&#2366;&#2312; &#2342;&#2375;&#2327;&#2368;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"216\" height=\"931\" id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8462/image023.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["II", "I", "III", "IV"], "options_hi": ["II", "I", "III", "IV"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><b>II</b> is the correct pattern obtained.</p><p>It is a transparent sheet, so the pattern on other side overlaps on the pattern on the side obtained. And the pattern on the side which is folded kind of reflects along the line along which it is folded.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>II</b> is the correct pattern obtained.</p><p>It is a transparent sheet, so the pattern on other side overlaps on the pattern on the side obtained. And the pattern on the side which is folded kind of reflects along the line along which it is folded.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the water image of the figure given below when a mirror is placed at the bottom of the figure:</p><p><img width=139 height=139 id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8605/image007.jpg\"></p><p><img width=299 height=612 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8605/image008.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2346;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2357;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p><img width=\"139\" height=\"139\" id=\"Picture 5\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8605/image007.jpg\"></p><p><img width=\"299\" height=\"612\" id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8605/image008.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=261 height=340 id=\"Picture 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8605/image009.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=261 height=340 id=\"Picture 13\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8605/image009.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Find out from amongst the four alternatives I, II, III and IV, as to how the pattern would appear on the sheet when the sheet is folded at the dotted line and is punched as shown.</p><p><img width=602 height=121 id=\"Picture 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p7841/image019.jpg\"></p><p><img width=218 height=629 id=\"Picture 28\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p7841/image020.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; I, II, III &#2324;&#2352; IV &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2351;&#2361; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2379;&#2396;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2351;&#2361; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2326;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;? </p><p><img width=\"602\" height=\"121\" id=\"Picture 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p7841/image019.jpg\"></p><p><img width=\"218\" height=\"629\" id=\"Picture 28\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p7841/image020.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["II", "I", "IV", "III"], "options_hi": ["II", "I", "IV", "III"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>On opening the paper fold by fold we get  - </p><p><img width=340 height=150 id=\"Picture 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p7841/image021.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>On opening the paper fold by fold we get  - </p><p><img width=340 height=150 id=\"Picture 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p7841/image021.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Select from the alternatives, the boxes that can be formed by folding the sheet shown in figure (X).</p><p><b><img width=262 height=152 id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20742/image006.jpg\"></b></p><p><b><img width=590 height=146 id=\"Picture 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20742/image007.jpg\"></b></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2344; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; (X) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2351;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><b><img width=\"262\" height=\"152\" id=\"Picture 21\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20742/image006.jpg\"></b></p><p><b><img width=\"590\" height=\"146\" id=\"Picture 22\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20742/image007.jpg\"></b></p>", "options_en": ["Only I, II and III", "Only III and IV", "Only I, II and IV", "Only II and III"], "options_hi": ["&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I, II &#2324;&#2352; III", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; III &#2324;&#2352; IV", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I, II &#2324;&#2352; IV", "&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II &#2324;&#2352; III"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><b><img width=245 height=100 id=\"Picture 23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20742/image008.jpg\"></b></p><p>Here in this figure  - </p><p>Face having 1 is opposite to face having 3.</p><p>Face having 4 is opposite to face having 6.</p><p>Face having 2 is opposite to face having 5.</p><p><b><img width=243 height=140 id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20742/image009.jpg\"></b></p><p>Thus, according to figure (X)  - </p><p>The face having shaded line is opposite to the face having rhombus figure. And they cannot be adjacent to each other.</p><p>The face with a star figure is opposite to the face with a Circle figure.</p><p>The face with a heptagon figure is opposite to the face with an Arrow figure.</p><p>Also, they are opposite to each other. They cannot be adjacent to each other.</p><p>Thus, only figure (II) and figure (III) will form by folding the sheet shown in figure (X).</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b><img width=245 height=100 id=\"Picture 23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20742/image008.jpg\"></b></p><p>Here in this figure  - </p><p>Face having 1 is opposite to face having 3.</p><p>Face having 4 is opposite to face having 6.</p><p>Face having 2 is opposite to face having 5.</p><p><b><img width=243 height=140 id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20742/image009.jpg\"></b></p><p>Thus, according to figure (X)  - </p><p>The face having shaded line is opposite to the face having rhombus figure. And they cannot be adjacent to each other.</p><p>The face with a star figure is opposite to the face with a Circle figure.</p><p>The face with a heptagon figure is opposite to the face with an Arrow figure.</p><p>Also, they are opposite to each other. They cannot be adjacent to each other.</p><p>Thus, only figure (II) and figure (III) will form by folding the sheet shown in figure (X).</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Select the correct mirror image of the given figure when mirror is placed at 'PQ' as shown. </p><p><img width=215 height=192 id=\"Picture 16\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18141/image015.png\"></p><p><img width=624 height=177 id=\"Picture 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18141/image016.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2346;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379; 'PQ' &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2360;&#2366;&#2352; &#2352;&#2326;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2346;&#2339; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2348; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"215\" height=\"192\" id=\"Picture 16\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18141/image015.png\"></p><p><img width=\"624\" height=\"177\" id=\"Picture 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18141/image016.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["I", "II", "III", "IV"], "options_hi": ["I", "II", "III", "IV"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Figure (II) would resemble the correct mirror image of the given figure. </p><p><img width=398 height=194 id=\"Picture 19\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18141/image017.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Figure (II) would resemble the correct mirror image of the given figure. </p><p><img width=398 height=194 id=\"Picture 19\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18141/image017.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Choose a figure which would most closely resemble the unfolded form of the last figure which shows the manner in which the folded paper has been cut. </p><p><img width=624 height=301 id=\"Drawing 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17133/image018.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2320;&#2360;&#2368; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2326;&#2369;&#2354;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368;-&#2332;&#2369;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360; &#2340;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2369;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2325;&#2366;&#2327;&#2332; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"624\" height=\"301\" id=\"Drawing 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17133/image018.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["I", "II", "III", "IV"], "options_hi": ["I", "II", "III", "IV"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Figure <b>(II)</b> is the correct unfolded figure.</p><p><img width=239 height=194 id=\"Drawing 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17133/image019.jpg\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Figure <b>(II)</b> is the correct unfolded figure.</p><p><img width=239 height=194 id=\"Drawing 18\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p17133/image019.jpg\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following will be the mirror image of the given figure (x), if the mirror is placed to its right. Choose the correct mirror image from given images (i), (ii), (iii) and (iv).</p><p><img width=236 height=90 id=\"Picture 26\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6512/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=614 height=212 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p6512/i